      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-14T15:50:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a huge security hole.\n\nThere is no other way to achieve what you need here without this?\n\nIf this is just for debugging, fine, but for a shipping device, watch out...",
      "parentUuid": "40193e3c_93556c8c",
      "revId": "8015459b0c27e54c6021be7ecc04d394674f414d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7373155_807125be",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1176763
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-14T15:58:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+security team\n\nPlease correct me, if I\u0027m wrong. I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a big hole, since UFS FW checks the binary integrity when doing FFU, and RPMB itself is a secured protocol which has the authentication. I\u0027m not sure what\u0027d be the point where those were already accessible from anywhere, but why not /dev/sgX.",
      "parentUuid": "ea1bada5_0707bef0",
      "revId": "8015459b0c27e54c6021be7ecc04d394674f414d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
